{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073ed91e1a9a1cda445af237b7b67815147c979.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JKLM$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" /> is drawn with its vertices on the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/a/b4a455d533200d7dfbd00731fa8bd9e8796fb803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bf1e5a1f898db422b11eb7246758290046d9386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PJ = PK = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"14\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/8/498d2203eeef25f0a4a2a64d57e8462925343e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$JQ = KR = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"18\" /> m, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf714d449b9c6ffe450fdbb57763660b3ee8f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> m, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1e54de87ff17f00d801c9de48ffd0dc0b15494.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> m, as shown\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 2 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f896d4530335912a46160e46d42a3681e99f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the diagram, we can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f896d4530335912a46160e46d42a3681e99f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> appears in the right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b091e2f5819e07742ad280d3f1505b245600c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(image of right triangle KLR specifically)\n</p><p>From here, we can then use the pythagorean theorem:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4bdaabf820cb52af199526a7e81be4e147779e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR^{2} + KL^{2} = KR^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/2/3f2ee54257479bbb73de804b6b7e897b540b8c79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR^{2} = KR^{2} - KL^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02ff1969a15998fdfdf095b4753822b4283b3326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR = \\sqrt{KR^{2} - KL^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"164\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc427b05e066e087d8d6b56e4132bf0333f8296b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KR = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf714d449b9c6ffe450fdbb57763660b3ee8f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c0a06a59e85a898baecff4ca4c14fe54acf6a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR = \\sqrt{50^{2} - 40^{2}} = \\sqrt{2500 - 1600}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"275\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373a3ecc9cb23b2ab5eb238c01ccfdfe99e051fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{900} = \\boxed{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"117\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>We could have also used difference of squares to achieve the answer:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3de86eea5da405b416eb56f738939d894ebfc02e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR = \\sqrt{50^{2} - 40^{2}} = \\sqrt{(50 + 40)(50 - 40)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"328\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aabe058316ad921f43f19379be9f88e76ae815b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{90 \\times 10} = \\sqrt{900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"161\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073eada80d26d83b64267cd2cb7b7c5d396508e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"50\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same right triangle from solution 1.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>However, instead of using the pythagorean theorem, we can realize that the triangle's side lengths must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times that of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> right triangle because the other leg and the hypotenuse are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as large as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> leg and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> leg.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3000c6f590410a4095f1fb5dc0a3d89a21bbdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LR = 10 \\times 3 = \\boxed{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"156\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012731\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 136/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1784/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4932/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.762      1 -total\n 83.70%   14.029      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n 34.17%    5.728      3 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35553:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012731 and revision id 277900. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}